=   refer hallucination.Canvas
-   refer hallucination.RasterOpenable
+   refer hallucination.RasterOpenable

-   entry .apply   `canvas(x, y)`: the typed pixel at a coordinate, through any open canvas
-       An extension on a handle granted `Read`, which every open canvas is: the same constant
-       shift and mask as the `pixel` extension on the raster, giving a `Pixel[layout]`.
-   entry .update   `canvas(x, y) = pixel`: writes a pixel in place, through a canvas opened with `Write`
-       An extension on a handle granted `Write` only: a canvas opened with `open[Canvas]()`
-       has no `update`, and the assignment does not compile. The write stores the pixel's
-       word directly into the raster's buffer, so it is seen by the raster itself and every
-       other reference to it, immediately.
-   entry #width   the width of the open raster
-   entry #height   the height of the open raster
-   entry #snapshot   an independent copy of the raster as it is now
-       A new `Raster by layout` with its own buffer, unaffected by writes made through the
-       canvas afterwards, for deriving an image from the state of a drawing without closing
-       it.
+   entry .apply   `canvas(x, y)`: el píxel tipado en una coordenada, mediante cualquier lienzo abierto
+       Una extensión sobre un descriptor con la concesión `Read`, que tiene todo lienzo abierto: el
+       mismo desplazamiento y la misma máscara constantes que la extensión `pixel` del ráster, que
+       dan un `Pixel[layout]`.
+   entry .update   `canvas(x, y) = pixel`: escribe un píxel in situ, mediante un lienzo abierto con `Write`
+       Una extensión solo sobre un descriptor con la concesión `Write`: un lienzo abierto con
+       `open[Canvas]()` no tiene `update`, y la asignación no compila. La escritura guarda la
+       palabra del píxel directamente en el búfer del ráster, así que la ven de inmediato el propio
+       ráster y cualquier otra referencia a él.
+   entry #width   la anchura del ráster abierto
+   entry #height   la altura del ráster abierto
+   entry #snapshot   una copia independiente del ráster tal como está ahora
+       Un `Raster by layout` nuevo con su propio búfer, al que no afectan las escrituras hechas
+       después mediante el lienzo, para derivar una imagen a partir del estado de un dibujo sin
+       cerrarlo.

- entry .RasterOpenable   the `Openable` instance class which opens a `Raster by layout` as a `Canvas`
+ entry .RasterOpenable   la clase de instancia de `Openable` que abre un `Raster by layout` como un `Canvas`

= entry .RasterOpenable   the `Openable` instance class which opens a `Raster by layout` as a `Canvas`
-   detail
+   detail

-       The typeclass instance behind `raster.open[Canvas](…)`: its `Self` is `Raster by
-       layout`, its `Form` is `Canvas`, it takes no flags (`Operand` is `Nothing`), and its
-       `Result` is `CanvasHandle[layout]`. It is a named class rather than an anonymous given
-       so that the handle's type is stated exactly; the given which supplies it is
-       `canvasOpenable`, which is what a program imports. Nothing is gained by naming this
-       class directly.
+       La instancia de la clase de tipos que hay detrás de `raster.open[Canvas](…)`: su `Self` es
+       `Raster by layout`, su `Form` es `Canvas`, no admite indicadores (`Operand` es `Nothing`) y
+       su `Result` es `CanvasHandle[layout]`. Es una clase con nombre y no un given anónimo, para
+       que el tipo del descriptor se indique con exactitud; el given que la proporciona es
+       `canvasOpenable`, que es lo que importa un programa. No se gana nada nombrando esta clase
+       directamente.

=       class directly.
-   refer hallucination.canvasOpenable
+   refer hallucination.canvasOpenable

-   entry #Self   `Raster by layout`: the raster type this opens
-   entry #Form   `Canvas`: the form the raster is opened as
-   entry #Operand   `Nothing`: a canvas takes no flags
-   entry #Result   `CanvasHandle[layout]`: the handle the block receives
-   entry #open   runs a block with a `CanvasHandle` over the raster, granted what the mode grants
-       Called by aperture's `open`: wraps the raster in a handle, refines it with the mode's
-       grants, and passes it to the block as a contextual value. The handle is new for each
-       open.
+   entry #Self   `Raster by layout`: el tipo de ráster que abre
+   entry #Form   `Canvas`: la forma como la que se abre el ráster
+   entry #Operand   `Nothing`: un lienzo no admite indicadores
+   entry #Result   `CanvasHandle[layout]`: el descriptor que recibe el bloque
+   entry #open   ejecuta un bloque con un `CanvasHandle` sobre el ráster, con las concesiones que otorga el modo
+       Lo llama el `open` de aperture: envuelve el ráster en un descriptor, lo refina con las
+       concesiones del modo y lo pasa al bloque como valor contextual. El descriptor es nuevo en
+       cada apertura.

- entry .canvasOpenable   the given which lets a `Raster by layout` be opened as a `Canvas`; import it by name
-     A top-level given in `hallucination.canvas`, so that decoding an image does not also
-     compile the scoped-resource machinery: it is not in implicit scope, and must be imported
-     as `import soundness.canvasOpenable` (or `import hallucination.canvasOpenable`). It
-     provides a `RasterOpenable[layout]` for every layout. Without it, `raster.open[Canvas]()`
-     fails to compile, since `Openable` has no generic fallback.
+ entry .canvasOpenable   el given que permite abrir un `Raster by layout` como un `Canvas`; se importa por nombre
+     Un given de nivel superior en `hallucination.canvas`, para que decodificar una imagen no
+     compile también la maquinaria de recursos con ámbito: no está en el ámbito implícito, y debe
+     importarse como `import soundness.canvasOpenable` (o `import hallucination.canvasOpenable`).
+     Proporciona un `RasterOpenable[layout]` para cada disposición. Sin él,
+     `raster.open[Canvas]()` no compila, ya que `Openable` no tiene ninguna alternativa genérica.

=     fails to compile, since `Openable` has no generic fallback.
